 "disposition": "ADMITTED_ON_DEMAND_DEPRIORITISED_ON_SERP_NOT_MATERIALISED",
 "disposition_reason": "The brief admits a market on measured demand AND real local phrasing AND a verified SERP. ko-KR passes the first two by the widest margin of any candidate and fails the third by the widest margin. So it is recorded as measured, kept out of the market list, and left unmaterialised. Three things would change that and none of them is a gate relaxation: a family whose Korean SERP is open that was not among the five sampled, a Naver-first distribution strategy that organic Google ranking is the wrong test for, or South Korea being captured and a domestic family measuring open. Until one of those, the pages would be built to rank behind Naver, and building 20,000 of them would add template mass to a site whose whole defence is that every page earns its place.",
 "correction_to_my_own_earlier_reading": "This market was committed as admitted at 576354a before any Korean SERP had been sampled, on the demand measurement alone. That was the wrong order of work: the SERP requirement exists precisely to catch a market like this one, and reading five SERPs cost 896 units and twenty minutes against a market that would have cost a capture, a mark pass and twenty thousand pages. The demand numbers in this file stand; the admission does not."
